          "text": "<teammate-message teammate_id=\"team-lead\">\nDiagnose and fix a Storybook 10.0 compatibility issue in storyproof, a Storybook visual-testing addon. Repo: /home/leon0399/Projects/storyproof (pnpm workspace). **All work via PR — never push to main, never merge, never git stash/reset/checkout--.**\n\n## Context you need\n\nAn open PR #2 (branch `task8-packed-consumer`, currently green, NOT yet merged) added a \"packed-consumer\" CI harness: it packs the real tarball, copies an example project out of the workspace, installs the tarball there, and runs a Playwright acceptance suite against a real Storybook. Base your work **on top of branch `task8-packed-consumer`** (not main — main is behind at `eedad1d`).\n\nThat harness found and fixed two real defects already. A third issue caused Storybook 10.0 support to be **abandoned**: the peer range was narrowed to `^10.5.0` and the `examples/react-vite-sb10.0` example plus its CI matrix cell were deleted. Read the release-plan deviation notes (`packages/storyproof/docs/2026-07-24-public-preview-release-plan.md`, search 2026-07-27) and the ROADMAP P1 bullet about the 10.0 floor for the full trail.\n\n**The symptom on Storybook 10.0.8 was:** panel renders correctly, the \"Run visual tests\" button is present/enabled/clickable, the click succeeds — but the panel **never reports any result**, so 8 of 11 acceptance tests timed out waiting for status text (\"New\"/\"Passed\"/\"Capture failed\"). The identical suite passes on 10.5.4 for both react-vite and nextjs-vite. A `@storybook/builder-vite` version-skew hypothesis was investigated and **ruled out** (`@storybook/react-vite@10.0.8` pins `builder-vite` to an exact version — verified via `pnpm why`). It was then filed as \"unexplained\".\n\n## The hypothesis to test (likely root cause, found by re-reading the evidence)\n\nA local run of the 10.0 example produced `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'getIndex')`, which was misattributed to the builder-vite skew. That error points at storyproof's own code:\n\n`src/preset.ts` (~line 55):\n```ts\nconst storyIndexGenerator = (await options.presets.apply(\n  \"storyIndexGenerator\",\n)) as StoryIndexGenerator;      // unchecked cast\n```\n`src/node/story-index.ts` (~line 16):\n```ts\nconst index = await generator.getIndex();   // throws exactly that error if generator is undefined\n```\n\n**Hypothesis:** on Storybook 10.0.8, `options.presets.apply(\"storyIndexGenerator\")` returns `undefined` (key absent / renamed / not populated in that minor). The unchecked `as` cast hides it at startup, and it explodes server-side the first time a run enumerates stories — producing exactly the observed signature: everything upstream fine, no result ever emitted.\n\n## Tasks\n\n**1. Diagnose (the decisive check).** Recreate a Storybook 10.0.8 consumer (the deleted `examples/react-vite-sb10.0` is recoverable from git history on this branch — `git log --diff-filter=D --name-only` to find the deleting commit, then `git show <sha>^:<path>`). Determine empirically what `options.presets.apply(\"storyIndexGenerator\")` returns inside `experimental_serverChannel` on 10.0.8 vs 10.5.4 — undefined, a different shape, or a throw. Log it from the preset during a real `storybook dev`. Note: Playwright cannot run on this WSL2 host (missing browser system libs), but the addon's server side runs fine under plain `storybook dev`, and the Chrome browser MCP tools are available if you need the UI. This diagnosis does NOT need Playwright.\n\n**2. Fix the underlying defect regardless of what step 1 finds.** Replace the unchecked `as` cast with a validated lookup that **fails closed at startup with an actionable error** — matching the pattern already in that same file (`optionError`, `resolveStoryRoots`, `resolveMaxConcurrency`: name the thing, say what was received, say what to do). Today a missing platform capability becomes an opaque 60-second hang with no diagnostic; it must become a clear startup failure naming the required Storybook capability. **This matters independently of 10.0** — if Storybook renames that preset key in any future minor, storyproof currently fails as a mystery timeout. Add a focused unit test for the new failure path (there are existing preset-validation tests in `test/server.test.ts` to model on).\n\n**3. Conditionally restore 10.0 support.** If step 1 reveals a clean path (the generator is available under another key, an alternative public API exists, or a small fallback works), restore `^10.0.0`: peer range, the `examples/react-vite-sb10.0` example, its CI matrix cell, and README / ROADMAP / release-plan wording. If there is no clean path, **keep `^10.5.0`** — but update the ROADMAP/release-plan entry to state the actual reason (\"Storybook 10.0.x does not expose `storyIndexGenerator` via presets\" or whatever you find) instead of \"unexplained\", and note that the new startup error now makes this fail loudly for anyone who tries.\n\n**Scope limits:** steps 1 and 2 unconditionally; step 3 only if step 1 shows a clean path. Do **not** reverse-engineer Storybook internals or build compatibility shims beyond identifying what that preset returns. If 10.0 needs real shimming, we stay at `^10.5.0` and the startup error does its job. No new bespoke scripts — this repo deliberately deleted seven of them in favor of conventional tooling.\n\n## Verification\n\nLocal (all must pass): `pnpm install`, `pnpm --filter storyproof build`, `pnpm --filter storyproof test`, `typecheck`, `lint`, `pnpm format:check`, `actionlint`, `zizmor .github/workflows/`, plus `pnpm --filter storyproof pack --out <tmp>/p.tgz` followed by `git diff --exit-code` (the generated package.json is a committed drift gate). Redirect long output to files under /tmp/claude-1000/-home-leon0399-Projects-llame/a398f1c1-a27d-4c74-8f62-94c24993161f/tasks/ and read the files — never pipe to head/grep. Then push and watch CI: `gh run watch <id> --repo leon0399/storyproof --exit-status`, and report **per-job** conclusions (`gh run view <id> --repo leon0399/storyproof --json jobs`).\n\n## Docs + PR\n\nUpdate the package `CHANGELOG.md` (Keep a Changelog `[Unreleased]`) and the release plan with a dated note recording that the earlier \"unexplained\" characterization was wrong — the evidence was sufficient, it was attributed to the wrong layer. Prettier-write only files you touch.\n\nPush to branch `task8-packed-consumer` if PR #2 is still open (fold these commits in — they belong with the work that found the issue). Conventional commits, with these trailers on each:\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011apGNwN6NEjPRtHLkX4YPF\n\nReport back: what the preset actually returns on each version, whether 10.0 is recoverable, what the new startup error says, per-job CI results, and anything uncertain.\n</teammate-message>",
